VCMI for RISC OS
================

VCMI is an open-source engine for Heroes of Might and Magic III (Shadow
of Death and Complete), the turn-based fantasy strategy game by New
World Computing (1999). It plays the original game with its maps and
campaigns, adds higher resolutions, a random map generator and many
interface improvements, and can load mods.

  VCMI:       https://vcmi.eu  https://github.com/vcmi/vcmi
  This port:  https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-vcmi

Version: see docs.Version.

This is a TEST BUILD
--------------------
It has not been tried on RISC OS hardware yet. Please report what
happens (see Problems below).

You need the original game
--------------------------
VCMI uses the pictures, sounds, music and maps of the original Heroes
III: Shadow of Death or Complete (GOG, CD). They aren't included. Copy
the Data, Maps and Mp3 directories into !VCMI.H3data: H3data.ReadMe
says how. Or keep them elsewhere and *Set VCMI$Data to their directory.

What you need
-------------
- RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine with VFP. A Raspberry Pi 4 is
  recommended: the computer players do a lot of thinking, and RISC OS
  gives the game one processor core.
- The ARMEABISupport module and SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later (from
  !PackMan) in !System.
- For sound: SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager, in ssb.zip on the
  RDPClient page: https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
  John Duffell's own site (now on the Internet Archive) has more details:
  https://web.archive.org/web/20110920080106/http://www.duffell.riscos.me.uk/
  Merge ssb.zip's !System with yours. SharedSound is part of RISC OS.
  Without them the game is silent.
- Several hundred MB of free memory (not measured yet).

Playing
-------
Double-click !VCMI. The game opens full screen (a desktop window that
covers the screen, so other programs keep running).

Settings, saved games and the log are kept in <Choices$Write>.VCMI.

Not in this port (yet)
----------------------
- The films (intro, and the ones in towns and campaigns).
- The launcher (VCMI's mod manager and data importer): mods have to be
  copied into <Choices$Write>.VCMI.Mods by hand.
- Online and network play.
- HD Edition graphics.

Problems
--------
Report them at https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-vcmi/issues with the
logs: <Choices$Write>.VCMI.Cache.VCMI_Client_log/txt, and vcmilog (see
!Run).

